Babel modifications (2026-10-08/09): strict-loaded original FP32 weights exported
into standard ONNX with fixed 641-frame spectral windows and two inference outputs.
Inference lowerings replace exporter-unsupported representations with numerically equivalent
standard operators. Query-partitioned all-key attention bounds intermediary
buffers without changing context, learned weights, or softmax rows. InstanceNorm
uses equivalent anchored two-pass mean/biased-variance reductions, retaining the
original epsilon and affine tensors to avoid near-constant FP32 cancellation.
Oversized Concat operations become ordered groups with at most seven inputs,
preserving values while fitting eight storage bindings per WebGPU shader.
Exact offline shape/index folding specializes the existing four-second runtime
contract. Compact shared row-major Gather indices replace replicated attention
GatherElements indices with identical tensor values and bounded constant storage.
No weights were trained, randomized, or taken from the publisher's separately
distributed ONNX. The original FP32 export and operator inventory remain in
models/zipenhancer.onnx and src/core/audio-enhancement-model.json for reproduction.
The packaged browser runtime uses a derived static plan and mixed-FP16 weight
storage, with FP32 sensitive nonlinearities, statistics, and matrix accumulation.
WGSL tiled all-key relative attention and exact source-DAG pointwise fusion
replace materialized intermediate operators; four-second context is unchanged.
Reproduction: scripts/export-zipenhancer.py and scripts/export-zipenhancer-webgpu.py.
Packaged assets and implementation identity: src/core/audio-enhancement-webgpu-model.json.

